# Real held filesystem locks; no source engine, provider or automatic work.
name: Scope inventory and history stay responsive during cross-process lock waits
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 20 Enter / c build inventory | empty-ready
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART start inventory
keys: c
require-live-snap: 20 Working · Ctrl+C cancel | inventory-waiting
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART inventory-waiting
ask: Does a held inventory lock leave the native TUI responsive with an explicit cancellation control and no scan or model approval?
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 Ctrl+C cancel | inventory-waiting-narrow
ask: At 40x12, is the active state and cancellation action readable without a stale completed result?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 20 Action stopped | inventory-canceled
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART inventory-canceled
ask: Does cancellation preserve the shell and publish no scope proposal while the other process still owns the lock?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART release inventory
resize: 120x36
keys: c
require-live-snap: 30 DRAFT SCOPES | recovered-inventory
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does explicit retry traverse a 300-level tree and wide empty directories into one whole-repository draft without forced subdivision?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART start strategy
keys: r
require-live-snap: 20 Working · Ctrl+C cancel | history-waiting
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART strategy-waiting
ask: Does refreshing scope history run in the background while keeping the selected saved boundary visible?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 20 Action stopped | history-canceled
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART strategy-canceled
ask: Does canceling a blocked history lookup retain the draft and leave the proposal queue untouched?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART release strategy
keys: r
require-live-snap: 20 PgUp/Dn read · a accept · Esc back | recovered-history
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_locks.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
keys: Escape
wait: 1
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 15 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | exit-confirmation
keys: y
require-exit: 10
